  "excerpt": "Whoopie pies are an American bake from the Pennsylvania Dutch tradition: two soft, dome-shaped chocolate cake rounds sandwiched with a fluffy cream-cheese filling. They are not a pie or a biscuit in the British sense but sit somewhere between a cookie and a small cake. The cake rounds are easy to make; the key is keeping them uniform in size so the sandwiches sit flat.",
