  "sourceNotes": "Whoopie pies are associated with the Pennsylvania Dutch community and Maine, where competing origin claims exist. The earliest printed recipe is often cited as a 1930 Durkee's Famous Foods recipe booklet; they appear in Pennsylvania Amish community cookbooks and charity collections from the mid-20th century onward. The name is thought to refer to the exclamation made when finding one in a lunch box. They became widely popular in mainstream American baking from the 1980s onward.",
