      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the batter"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 180°C (conventional). Line two large baking trays with baking paper. Sift {{plain-flour}}, {{cocoa-powder}}, {{bicarbonate-of-soda}}, {{baking-powder}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}} into a bowl. In a separate bowl, whisk {{caster-sugar}}, {{vegetable-oil}}, {{eggs}}, and {{vanilla-extract}} until pale and combined. Fold in the flour mixture alternately with {{whole-milk}}, beginning and ending with flour. Mix until just smooth; do not overbeat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Scoop and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Drop heaped tablespoons of batter onto the lined trays, spacing them 5 cm apart to allow for spreading. You are aiming for rounds about 6 cm across and slightly domed. Bake for 12 to 14 minutes until the rounds spring back when pressed lightly in the centre and a skewer comes out clean. Cool completely on wire racks before filling; 30 minutes minimum."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the filling and assemble"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beat {{cream-cheese}} with {{icing-sugar}} and {{vanilla-extract}} until smooth and fluffy. Spread or pipe generously onto the flat side of half the rounds, then sandwich with the remaining rounds, flat-side down. Press lightly to spread the filling to the edges."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
